# Source of truth for backend dependencies -- loose constraints, human-edited.
#
# requirements.txt is GENERATED from this file and is fully pinned with hashes.
# Do not edit requirements.txt by hand -- the Dockerfile installs it with
# --require-hashes, so a hand-edited entry fails the build.
#
# To change a dependency: edit this file, then regenerate from backend/ with
#
#   uv pip compile requirements.in -o requirements.txt --generate-hashes \
#     --python-version 3.11 --python-platform x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
#
# The --python-version / --python-platform flags target the runtime image
# (python:3.11-slim, linux/amd64) rather than the developer's machine, so the
# pins are the ones that will actually be installed. Without them, a macOS
# checkout resolves platform-specific wheels (psycopg2-binary, uvloop) wrong.

